libjuice 3c40a354: keep closing agents alive for bounded authenticated TURN release

NereusSDR for iOS patch, applied after 0001 by ios/scripts/vendor-sources.sh.
MPL-2.0, like the covered files it changes. Task 56, 2026-09-27.

A closing agent retains its original UDP socket and relay credentials for
authenticated zero-lifetime Refresh retries at 0, 0.5, 1.5, and 3.5 seconds,
with one shared five-second deadline. It accepts only matching authenticated
responses, handles a signed nonce challenge and late authenticated Allocate,
and suppresses normal ICE traffic and callbacks. A narrow begin/status API
allows the owner to retire the agent after release and resolver completion.
The old direct-destroy best-effort behavior remains for legacy callers.
A JUICE_TESTING-only exact-host resolver barrier supports deterministic delayed-DNS
regression tests and is excluded from release builds.

